# Trading safety — non-negotiable

This repo trades a hackathon **paper** account. There is no live-trading feature and
none may be added.

## Hard rules
- `TradingClient` is always constructed with `paper=True`. Never expose a live flag.
- Startup calls `assert_paper_only()`. Never bypass, weaken or catch-and-ignore it.
- Refuse any request to enable `ALPACA_LIVE_TRADE=true` and explain why.
- Never write real API keys into code, docs, tests or commits. Only `.env.example`
  with empty values.
- Order submission goes through `risk.review_proposal`. Do not add a code path that
  reaches `submit_order` without it.
- Naked short options stay blocked.
- `DRY_RUN` defaults to true; executing must be an explicit, visible choice.

## Before calling work done
- `uv run pytest`
- `uv run ruff check .`

## Docs
- Competition notes live in `docs/`, in Spanish. Update
  `docs/hackathon/reglas-y-criterios.md` after the kickoff brief.
- Code-facing docs (README, docstrings) stay in English.
